  "articleBody": "Installing door casing might seem straightforward, but a few common mistakes can really impact the final look. One frequent error is using pieces that are too short or not perfectly square. This often leads to visible gaps at the corners or between the casing and the door jamb. Always measure carefully and double-check your cuts! Another pitfall is failing to account for uneven jambs or walls. Most homes aren't perfectly plumb, and trying to force straight casing onto an uneven surface will result in unsightly gaps. Sometimes, you need to make slight adjustments or use shims to get everything aligned just right. Leaving visible gaps at the miters is a dead giveaway of a DIY job, so taking the time to ensure tight, precise corner joints is crucial. Finally, don't overlook the importance of the final finish work, like filling nail holes and caulking seams. These small details make a huge difference in achieving a professional look. If precision trim work isn't your strong suit, or if you have challenging openings, consider bringing in a professional. HH Remodeling LLC specializes in detailed interior finish work and can ensure your door casing looks flawless throughout your Denver area home.",
